{
    "attributes": {
        "action": "Apologise for Britain\u2019s role in the Partition of British India in 1947",
        "additional_details": "For hundreds of years, diverse communities in India co-existed prior to the British colonisation of India, which lasted over 200 years. We feel British rulers separated Hindus and Muslims into different political groups, which resulted in religious identity becoming more important than a shared national identity.\r\n \r\nWe believe that Britain, which was bankrupt after the Second World War and eager to withdraw, introduced the Indian Independence Act 1947 and asked a British lawyer to draw the new border, leading to the Partition, which caused mass migration, regional disparities and impacted millions of lives.",
        "background": "We call on the Prime Minister to issue a formal apology for Britain\u2019s role in the Partition of British India in 1947, and for the innocent lives that were lost, which is estimated to be up to 2 million.",
